{"id": "601442f5-a175-4d8e-9df9-69767dbd4a24", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T16:03:30.168403", "source": "user", "parent_id": "5ee43f45-53a3-4779-b6bd-0dbaebeaefa1", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"At this initial inspection stage, do not produce the full experiment design yet. Please report back with the following three items only, and keep the response concise (single JSON object would be ideal, otherwise a short structured response): 1) Repository inspection — list the contents of /workspace (top-level and any directly relevant subdirectories such as the one implementing zero bubble pipeline parallelism). For the files most relevant to 1F1B, 1F1B-I, ZB-1p, and ZB-2p scheduling, report their paths and a brief description of what each contains (e.g., the schedule logic, timing/bubble accounting, any existing benchmarks or simulation harnesses). 2) Proposed approach — outline the high-level design you propose for the experiment that answers the throughput-vs-microbatch-count question for {1F1B, 1F1B-I, ZB-1p, ZB-2p}, including: what variable you sweep (microbatch count M), what you hold fixed (pipeline depth, per-stage compute/communication cost model, batch size, etc.), how you measure throughput, what comparators you include, and whether the experiment will be an analytical/simulation model derived from the repo's formulas or a runtime emulation. Explicitly flag any choices that could materially change the answer (e.g., assumption of symmetric stages, ignoring warm-up/cooldown, modeling cross-mesh communication cost). 3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties — list the assumptions baked into your proposed design (cost-model fidelity, what 'throughput' means here — steady-state tokens/sec vs. end-to-end makespan, how microbatches interact with the schedule) and any repository or environmental unknowns (no GPU, no networking, dependency install status, Python/system-only setup) that could constrain feasibility. Do not yet produce the full design, controls, analysis plan, or feasibility rationale — those will be requested after I review this proposal.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the throughput for methods 1F1B, 1F1B-I, and ZB-1p improve as the number of microbatches increases, while ZB-2p maintains high throughput even with fewer microbatches? (Note: These methods are implemented as part of the zero bubble pipeline parallelism strategies in this repository, which aim to reduce pipeline bubbles and maintain high throughput.)\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
